<LegalLayout
  title="Cookie Policy"
  description="Cookie Policy for VixenBliss Agency, explaining cookies, similar technologies, user controls, and contact details."
>
  <p>
    This Cookie Policy explains how VixenBliss Agency may use cookies and similar technologies on the public website.
    The site is designed as a fast, mobile-friendly creative media experience, and some browser technologies may be used
    to keep pages reliable, media responsive, and the overall experience consistent.
  </p>
  <p>
    We keep our cookie approach focused on practical website needs. We do not require visitors to create an account to
    browse public pages, and we aim to avoid unnecessary complexity in the browsing experience.
  </p>

  <h2>What Cookies Are</h2>
  <p>
    Cookies are small text files that a website can place on your device through your browser. Similar technologies may
    include local storage, session storage, pixels, server logs, or content delivery signals. These tools can help a
    website remember simple information, load content efficiently, measure technical performance, and protect against
    misuse.
  </p>
  <p>
    Some cookies are set directly by the site you are visiting. Others may be set by service providers that help deliver
    media, host content, manage infrastructure, or measure aggregate performance.
  </p>

  <h2>How We Use Cookies</h2>
  <p>
    VixenBliss Agency may use cookies or similar technologies to operate the website, support media playback, preserve
    basic preferences, improve loading speed, understand general navigation patterns, diagnose errors, and maintain site
    security. These uses help us provide a stable experience across modern browsers and devices.
  </p>
  <p>
    For example, technical signals may help determine whether a page loaded correctly, whether a video asset was
    delivered successfully, or whether a public route generated an error. Aggregate interaction data may help us improve
    layout clarity, campaign quality, and mobile performance.
  </p>

  <h2>Types of Cookies</h2>
  <p>
    Technical cookies are used to make the website function correctly. They may support page loading, media delivery,
    browser compatibility, routing, security, and basic service reliability.
  </p>
  <p>
    Preference cookies may be used to remember simple choices, such as interface behavior or browser-based settings,
    where applicable. These preferences are intended to improve usability without requiring a visitor account.
  </p>
  <p>
    Performance cookies or similar aggregate signals may be used to understand how the website performs, which pages are
    viewed, and whether visitors encounter technical issues. These tools help us improve site speed, accessibility, and
    presentation quality.
  </p>
  <p>
    Third-party service technologies may be used by providers involved in content delivery, hosting, video streaming, or
    content management. For example, Bunny may support video delivery and Directus may support content management.
    These providers may process limited technical information as part of delivering their services.
  </p>

  <h2>User Control</h2>
  <p>
    You can manage cookies through your browser settings. Most browsers allow you to block cookies, delete existing
    cookies, limit third-party cookies, or receive alerts before cookies are stored. Browser controls vary, so review
    your browser's help documentation for the most accurate instructions.
  </p>
  <p>
    If cookies or similar storage are blocked, some technical behavior may change. Pages may still load, but certain
    features, preferences, media behavior, or performance measurements may not work in the same way.
  </p>

  <h2>Operational Signals</h2>
  <p>
    Some information connected to cookies or similar technologies may be processed as operational signals rather than
    stored as long-term visitor profiles. These signals can help identify slow pages, failed media requests, routing
    errors, or unusual traffic patterns that affect reliability.
  </p>
  <p>
    We use this type of information to maintain a professional public experience and to understand broad site behavior.
    Where possible, we prefer aggregate or technical context over information that directly identifies a visitor.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes to This Policy</h2>
  <p>
    We may update this Cookie Policy as the website changes, as providers are added or removed, or as browser technology
    evolves. The updated version will be posted on this page with a revised date.
  </p>
  <p>
    We recommend reviewing this page periodically if you want to stay informed about how cookies and similar
    technologies are used on the website.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>
    For questions about cookies, browser technologies, privacy, or legal requests, contact
    <a href="mailto:support@vixenbliss.com">support@vixenbliss.com</a>.
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
